<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>ComicCraft - Requirement Analysis</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #eef2ff;
      color: #1e1b4b;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 20px;
    }
    .container {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 20px auto;
      background: white;
      padding: 25px;
      border-radius: 15px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 15px #0001;
    }
    h1 { color: #4338ca; text-align: center; }
    h2 { color: #3730a3; }
    .item {
      padding: 12px;
      margin: 10px 0;
      background: #eef2ff;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }
    button {
      padding: 12px 18px;
      background: #4338ca;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 8px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    #result { line-height: 1.7; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="container">
    <h1>ComicCraft</h1>
    <h2>Phase 2: Requirement Analysis</h2>

    <p>This phase identifies the requirements needed
    to develop an AI Comic Story Creator.</p>

    <h2>1. Functional Requirements</h2>
    <div class="item">User can enter a story prompt.</div>
    <div class="item">The application can generate a comic story using AI.</div>
    <div class="item">Generated story scenes can be displayed.</div>
    <div class="item">Illustrations can be added through a supported image service.</div>

    <h2>2. Software Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Python</li>
      <li>JavaScript, HTML and CSS</li>
      <li>Gemini API access</li>
      <li>Web browser</li>
      <li>GitHub for source code management</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Hardware Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Computer or smartphone</li>
      <li>Internet connection for online AI services</li>
      <li>Modern web browser</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. User Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Simple and user-friendly interface</li>
      <li>Clear story output</li>
      <li>Useful error messages</li>
    </ul>

    <button onclick="showSummary()">View Requirements Summary</button>
    <p id="result" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </main>

  <script>
    function showSummary() {
      document.getElementById("result").textContent =
        "ComicCraft requires a user interface, a backend, " +
        "Gemini API access, and a browser to generate and " +
        "display AI-assisted comic stories.";
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
